I.O[1879422516] = { { "Leitstáth", "Leitstáth", "After overcoming the forces of the Iron Crown at Rathad Caul, the Narrow Way, an expedition of Zhélruka under orders from Prince Ingór established the camp of Leitstáth in Câr Bronach. After the...", "After overcoming the forces of the Iron Crown at Rathad Caul, the Narrow Way, an expedition of Zhélruka under orders from Prince Ingór established the camp of Leitstáth in Câr Bronach. After the..." }, { "Crágan Bris", "Crágan Bris", "Destroyed when the Witch-king of Angmar sought dominion over Câr Bronach, Crágan Bris was once a village of stone-giants of the Grímklettar clan. After the Grímklettar were displaced from their...", "Destroyed when the Witch-king of Angmar sought dominion over Câr Bronach, Crágan Bris was once a village of stone-giants of the Grímklettar clan. After the Grímklettar were displaced from their..." }, { "Grúmachath", "Grúmachath", "Built long ago when the kingdom of Angmar still spanned lands as far to the east as Câr Bronach, Grúmachath was once a fortified outpost of the Iron Crown. Captured in recent days by the Zhélruka...", "Built long ago when the kingdom of Angmar still spanned lands as far to the east as Câr Bronach, Grúmachath was once a fortified outpost of the Iron Crown. Captured in recent days by the Zhélruka..." }, { "Eiglinn", "Eiglinn", "Once a shimmering lake in the western heights of Ered Mithrin, Eiglinn has been defiled by the Angmarim of the Iron Crown. An unexpected by-product of fell sorcery and experimentation at Tûr Fúar,...", "Once a shimmering lake in the western heights of Ered Mithrin, Eiglinn has been defiled by the Angmarim of the Iron Crown. An unexpected by-product of fell sorcery and experimentation at Tûr Fúar,..." }, { "Clavanail", "Clavanail", "Driven from their homes in the glen after the Iron Crown fled Angmar, many of the birds of Câr Bronach now nest in the rocky heights of Clavanail, save, of course, for carrion-birds, who now feast...", "Driven from their homes in the glen after the Iron Crown fled Angmar, many of the birds of Câr Bronach now nest in the rocky heights of Clavanail, save, of course, for carrion-birds, who now feast..." }, { "Eiricháv", "Eiricháv", "After the fall of Angmar, dissent grew within the Hill-men of the Trév Duvárdain. Although many of their kin still serve the Iron Crown, a growing number of Hill-men have abandoned their wicked...", "After the fall of Angmar, dissent grew within the Hill-men of the Trév Duvárdain. Although many of their kin still serve the Iron Crown, a growing number of Hill-men have abandoned their wicked..." } }
