I.O[1879513793] = { { "The Haunt of Kidu-bâla", "The Haunt of Kidu-bâla", "Kidu-bâla, or 'rebel-covert', is a cliff-side camp of brigands and Ordâkhai deserters who have declared independence from the laws of both the empire and any upstart kingdoms who claim dominion over...", "Kidu-bâla, or 'rebel-covert', is a cliff-side camp of brigands and Ordâkhai deserters who have declared independence from the laws of both the empire and any upstart kingdoms who claim dominion over..." }, { "Duríga", "Duríga", "The brigands at Duríga, or 'gleaners' cleft', survive by assaulting Ordâkhai patrols and stealing the rations from the escaped thralls hiding in the ruins of Dur Nâgu.", "The brigands at Duríga, or 'gleaners' cleft', survive by assaulting Ordâkhai patrols and stealing the rations from the escaped thralls hiding in the ruins of Dur Nâgu." }, { "Fane of Shahûru", "Fane of Shahûru", "Shahûru, or 'shrine on a summit', is all that remains of an ancient Nêshak temple where the local people left offerings, praying for abundant harvests and the blessings of rain. The identity of the...", "Shahûru, or 'shrine on a summit', is all that remains of an ancient Nêshak temple where the local people left offerings, praying for abundant harvests and the blessings of rain. The identity of the..." }, { "Gnasher's Delf", "Gnasher's Delf", "Gnasher's Delf, or 'Haraz Hûr', is just the top of a large grodbog hive. They thrive in the cliffs because of deep cracks in the rock that lead to ground water, opened by the Din of Stone over a...", "Gnasher's Delf, or 'Haraz Hûr', is just the top of a large grodbog hive. They thrive in the cliffs because of deep cracks in the rock that lead to ground water, opened by the Din of Stone over a..." }, { "Nax Shalâl", "Nax Shalâl", "Nax Shalâl, or 'the Slithering Pit', is a recessed oasis, hidden in the cliffs. What would be a refuge for the people of Idagâl has become too dangerous to go near, as the local cobra population has...", "Nax Shalâl, or 'the Slithering Pit', is a recessed oasis, hidden in the cliffs. What would be a refuge for the people of Idagâl has become too dangerous to go near, as the local cobra population has..." }, { "Ushumût", "Ushumût", "Ushumût, or the Grave of Serpents, is the remains of three massive dragons and home to the wild-drakes of Idagâl. The Beltáni have passed down the tale of the fall of these dragons, named Ahûshu,...", "Ushumût, or the Grave of Serpents, is the remains of three massive dragons and home to the wild-drakes of Idagâl. The Beltáni have passed down the tale of the fall of these dragons, named Ahûshu,..." }, { "The Wither-watch", "The Wither-watch", "The Wither-watch, or Okhatohól, was once a thriving Shagâni town overlooking the river Agâl. The Din of Stone, the drying of the lake, and the invasion by the Ordâkhai slowly left the town nearly...", "The Wither-watch, or Okhatohól, was once a thriving Shagâni town overlooking the river Agâl. The Din of Stone, the drying of the lake, and the invasion by the Ordâkhai slowly left the town nearly..." }, { "Jolakhúro", "Jolakhúro", "Jolakhúro, or 'notch of the tunnel', is the Ordâkhai forward camp that watches the road to their main fortress at Emax Dûl. The soldiers there watch for approaching enemies, and are the first sent...", "Jolakhúro, or 'notch of the tunnel', is the Ordâkhai forward camp that watches the road to their main fortress at Emax Dûl. The soldiers there watch for approaching enemies, and are the first sent..." }, { "Emax Dûl", "Emax Dûl", "Emax Dûl, 'high hall of the cleft', or the High-hold, is an ancient fortress that has stood through the rise and fall of the many dynasties of both Nêshak and Nísaka. It is now the seat of power of...", "Emax Dûl, 'high hall of the cleft', or the High-hold, is an ancient fortress that has stood through the rise and fall of the many dynasties of both Nêshak and Nísaka. It is now the seat of power of..." }, { "Karmu Râx", "Karmu Râx", "Karmu Râx, or 'the mound of the turtles', is the gathering place for many dread-tortoises along the trickle that remains of the river Agâl. The shallow water and shelter provided by old wrecks from...", "Karmu Râx, or 'the mound of the turtles', is the gathering place for many dread-tortoises along the trickle that remains of the river Agâl. The shallow water and shelter provided by old wrecks from..." }, { "The Scardelve", "The Scardelve", "The Scardelve, or 'Góbor-noti', is the remains of an old pit mine carved from the cliff by the Ordâkhai. Once the ore ran dry, it became a holding pen for Mûmakil. As the Ordâkhai began to lose...", "The Scardelve, or 'Góbor-noti', is the remains of an old pit mine carved from the cliff by the Ordâkhai. Once the ore ran dry, it became a holding pen for Mûmakil. As the Ordâkhai began to lose..." }, { "Tombs of Khâb Ishil", "Tombs of Khâb Ishil", "Khâb Ishil, or 'the tomb of shards', is the ancient burial house of heroes from the kingdoms of Nêshak and Nísaka. It was long ago sealed and left untouched for hundreds of years. The Din of Stone...", "Khâb Ishil, or 'the tomb of shards', is the ancient burial house of heroes from the kingdoms of Nêshak and Nísaka. It was long ago sealed and left untouched for hundreds of years. The Din of Stone..." }, { "Esh Mêkag Pit-mine", "Esh Mêkag Pit-mine", "Esh Mêkag, 'the Silent Mouth', is an ancient Nêshakari fortress built into the stone cliffs of the Mûr. In recent years, the Ordâkhai have turned the fortress into a horrific prison and work-camp....", "Esh Mêkag, 'the Silent Mouth', is an ancient Nêshakari fortress built into the stone cliffs of the Mûr. In recent years, the Ordâkhai have turned the fortress into a horrific prison and work-camp...." } }
